        {
          "path": "_m/g/f/7/3/scalpay-outer-hebrides-wp/scalpay-fish-processing-factor.jpg",
          "filename": "Scalpay Fish Processing Factory -now closed - geograph.org.uk - 131326.jpg",
          "caption": "Scalpay Fish Processing Factory -now closed. The 2880 sq. m plant, operational from March 2001 to early 2005, was constructed by Highlands and Islands Enterprise and was being rented by Stolt Sea Farms on a 20 yr lease. The £10m development is expected to provide 109 full time equivalent jobs, with investment of £4.5m by HIE. Following a merger of Stolt the factory was closed after only 4 years. Fish is now processed on the mainland. There is hope that the factory will re-open for the processing of mussels, should the proposed farm on Taransay go ahead.",
          "alt": "Scalpay Fish Processing Factory -now closed. The 2880 sq. m plant, operational from March 2001 to early 2005, was constructed by Highlands and Islands Enterprise and was being rented by Stolt Sea Farms on a 20 yr lease. The £10m development is expected to provide 109 full time equivalent jobs, with investment of £4.5m by HIE. Following a merger of Stolt the factory was closed after only 4 years. Fish is now processed on the mainland. There is hope that the factory will re-open for the processing of mussels, should the proposed farm on Taransay go ahead.",
          "width": 640,
          "height": 480,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "David Wake",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Scalpay_Fish_Processing_Factory_-now_closed_-_geograph.org.uk_-_131326.jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
          "sourceArticleId": "scalpay-outer-hebrides-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "gf73",
          "smallPath": "_m/g/f/7/3/scalpay-outer-hebrides-wp/scalpay-fish-processing-factor-small.webp"
        },
        {
